  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Variant_decodeJsonUnwrapExtensionObject",
    "file": "open62541/src/ua_types_encoding_json.c",
    "description": "On the structure-unwrapping path, the function assigns `dst->type` and an allocated object to `dst->data`. If `decodeFields` then fails, it calls `UA_free(dst->data)` but leaves `dst->data` dangling (and `dst->type` intact). The error propagates to `UA_decodeJson`, whose generic `UA_deleteMembers` cleanup interprets the dangling allocation according to that type and frees/clears it again. In this PoV it treats the freed object as a `LocalizedText`; `String_clear` reads its freed string fields, producing the heap-use-after-free. The failure path must either perform typed cleanup and reset the Variant, or at minimum ensure no dangling owned pointer remains before returning.",
    "conditions": "Decode attacker-controlled JSON as a `UA_Variant` whose `Type` is ExtensionObject (22). Its `Body` must contain a valid `TypeId` resolving to a known structured datatype, causing `Variant_decodeJsonUnwrapExtensionObject` to set the Variant type and allocate `dst->data`, followed by body content that fails decoding. The PoV uses `TypeId.Id` 21 (`LocalizedText`) and an array `[]` where the structured LocalizedText body is expected; the malformed separator syntax is nevertheless tokenized sufficiently to reach this path. `decodeFields` returns an error after allocation, the function raw-frees but does not null `dst->data`, and top-level error cleanup dereferences/frees that stale pointer."
  },
